0	section	Getting washed down the waterfall after talking to Hudon
1	line	Gerald	Blimey! Where did you come from? Not another one of those treasure hunters are you?
1	line	Player	Treasure hunters?
1	line	Gerald	They say there's treasure hidden within the waterfall, left behind by the old elven king. Not that anyone's ever found anything.
1	line	Player	Interesting, is there somewhere I can learn more about this?
1	line	Gerald	You could ask Hadley the tourist guide. He'll be in this building just here.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to Almera after talking to Hudon
1	line	Player	Hello again.
1	line	Almera	Well hello, you're still around then.
1	line	Player	I saw Hudon by the river but he refused to come back with me.
1	line	Almera	Yes he told me, the foolish lad came in drenched to the bone, he had fallen into the waterfall, lucky he wasn't killed! Now he can spend the rest of the summer in his room.
1	line	Player	Any ideas what I could do while I'm here?
1	line	Almera	Why don't you visit the tourist centre south of the waterfall?
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to Gerald again before learning about the treasure
1	line	Player	Hello.
1	line	Gerald	Hello traveller. Are you here to fish or to hunt for treasure?
1	line	Player	Why do you say that?
1	line	Gerald	Adventurers pass through here every week, they never find anything though.
1	line	Player	What treasure are they looking for?
1	line	Gerald	They say there's treasure hidden within the waterfall, left behind by the old elven king. Not that anyone's ever found anything.
1	line	Player	Interesting, is there somewhere I can learn more about this?
1	line	Gerald	You could ask Hadley the tourist guide. He'll be in this building just here.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to Hadley
1	line	Player	Hello there.
1	cond	If the player doesn't have the Book on Baxtorian in their inventory:
2	line	Hadley	Are you on holiday? If so you've come to the right place. I'm Hadley the tourist guide, anything you need to know just ask me. We have some of the most unspoilt wildlife and scenery in Gielinor.
2	line	Hadley	People come from miles around to fish in the clear lakes or to wander the beautiful hillsides.
2	line	Player	It is quite pretty.
2	line	Hadley	Surely pretty is an understatement, [sir./lady./.] Beautiful, amazing or possibly life-changing would be more suitable wording. Have you seen Baxtorian Falls? Named after the elven king who was buried beneath them.
2	action	continues
1	cond	If the player has the Book on Baxtorian in their inventory:
2	line	Hadley	I hope you're enjoying your stay, there should be lots of useful infomation in that book you've got. Make sure you give it a read.
2	action	continues
1	select	Select an option
1	option	Can you tell me what happened to the elven king?
2	line	Player	Can you tell me what happened to the elven king?
2	line	Hadley	Baxtorian? I guess he died a long long time ago, it's quite sad really. After leaving his kingdom to deal with invading forces, Baxtorian returned to find his wife Glarial had been captured by the enemy.
2	line	Hadley	This destroyed Baxtorian, after years of searching he became a recluse. He went into the secret home he had made for Glarial under the waterfall and sealed himself in. To this day, no one has managed to enter.
2	line	Hadley	Anyway, I believe we have a book on him upstairs if you want to learn more.
2	action	other
1	option	Where else is worth visiting around here?
2	line	Player	Where else is worth visiting around here?
2	line	Hadley	There is a lovely spot for a picnic on the hill to the north east, there's a monument to the elven queen Glarial. It really is quite pretty.
2	line	Player	Who was Glarial?
2	line	Hadley	Baxtorian's wife, the only other person who could also enter the waterfall apart from him. She was queen when this land was inhabited by elven kind.
2	line	Hadley	Glarial was kidnapped while Baxtorian was away, but they eventually recovered her body and brought her home to rest.
2	line	Player	That's sad.
2	line	Hadley	True, I believe we have a book on Baxtorian and Glarial upstairs if you want to learn more.
2	action	other
1	option	Is there treasure under the waterfall?
2	line	Player	Is there treasure under the waterfall?
2	line	Hadley	Ha ha... Another treasure hunter. Well if there is no one's been able to get to it. They've been searching that river for decades, all to no avail.
2	action	other
1	option	Thanks, goodbye.
2	line	Player	Thanks, goodbye.
2	line	Hadley	Enjoy your visit.
2	action	end
